<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Japanese. The English source is quoted above each entry so a reviewer never has to hold two files
    open at once. Terms are fixed by docs/i18n/ja-glossary.md — HiLight, LED and JSON stay in Latin
    script, 常時点灯スタイル is the always-on look, and 1 周期の時間 is the cycle duration.

    Register: polite-neutral です・ます for captions addressed to the reader; slider labels, toggle
    labels, buttons and badges are noun phrases with no full stop.

    Length: the slider labels share their row with a value badge and the three-button rows are equal
    width with no wrapping, so Export and Import are 書き出し / 読み込み rather than the katakana
    forms, which would be ellipsised.
-->
